<title>AUSTRIA: SKIFLYING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SKIFLYING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BAD MITTERNDORF, Austria 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the</p>
<p>final day of the World Cup ski-flying competition on Sunday:</p>
<p> 1. Primoz Peterka (Slovenia) 386.2 points (195.5/203.0 metres)</p>
<p> 2. Andreas Goldberger (Austria)	    379.2 (195.5/200.5)</p>
<p> 3. Takanobu Okabe (Japan)		    376.3 (195.5/193.5)</p>
<p> 4. Janne Ahonen (Finland)		    373.4 (192.5/192.0)</p>
<p> 5. Lasse Ottesen (Norway)		    361.7 (186.5/189.5)</p>
<p> 6. Kazuyoshi Funaki (Japan)		  358.5 (194.5/178.0)</p>
<p> 7. Tommy Ingebrigtsen (Norway)	     351.3 (185.5/183.5)</p>
<p> 8. Jani Soininen (Finland)		   351.2 (177.5/196.0)</p>
<p> 9. Haarvard Lie (Norway)		     350.0 (182.0/190.5)</p>
<p> 10.Akira Higashi (Japan)		     348.1 (173.5/197.0)</p>
<p>World standings (after 19 events):</p>
<p> 1. Peterka			 1,097 points</p>
<p> 2. Dieter Thoma (Germany)	984</p>
<p> 3. Goldberger			817</p>
<p> 4. Okabe			     800</p>
